{# An American-style "work in progress" barricade planted on a zone under works
   (§ délais): a hazard-striped board on two splayed legs, its dark centre plate
   captioned with the phase. `phase` picks the local variant class (CVA-manuel,
   cf. CLAUDE.md §7) AND the caption: both phases are fully opaque — planned
   ("Travaux / à venir", during the lead: a chantier is reserved here, also why
   some tree choices are blocked) is static; active ("Travaux / en cours", the
   pose: the artisan is on site) gets a flashing amber beacon and a slight bob.
   Origin = ground midpoint between the two feet; the board stands above it.
   Colours/motion live in scene.css. Non-clickable (pointer-events none) so the
   zone underneath stays selectable. #}
{% props phase = 'planned' %}
{% set line2 = phase == 'active' ? 'en cours' : 'à venir' %}
<g class="chantier-marker chantier-marker--{{ phase }}"{{ attributes }}>
    <path class="cm-legs" d="M-14 -12 L-26 0 M14 -12 L26 0"/>
    <rect class="cm-board" x="-34" y="-42" width="68" height="30" rx="3"/>
    <rect class="cm-plate" x="-30" y="-38" width="60" height="22" rx="2"/>
    <circle class="cm-beacon" cx="0" cy="-46" r="3"/>
    <text class="cm-label" text-anchor="middle">
        <tspan x="0" y="-29">Travaux</tspan>
        <tspan x="0" y="-20">{{ line2 }}</tspan>
    </text>
</g>
